     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as 850 mg three times daily. Twice that amount raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function. It may be a typo, for example 850 mg or 1000 mg instead of 1700 mg.\n\n2. **A prescriber needs to place it.** You've said you aren't a clinician. A licensed prescriber who is treating this patient should enter or authorize medication orders.\n\nIf the treating clinician confirms the intended dose, I can enter it right away. For example, metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day. I can also enter it if the prescriber gives me a dose and explicitly confirms it."
      }
