     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** It comes to 5,100 mg/day, twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day. The risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is the same whoever confirms it.\n- **You aren't a prescriber.** A confirmation from a non-clinician doesn't replace a prescriber's order.\n\nHere are options that would work:\n- **The treating prescriber enters or confirms the order.** If they really intend a dose above the standard maximum, they should document the clinical reason. Pharmacy would probably review it too.\n- **I enter a standard dose once a prescriber specifies it.** One example is metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Pharmacy or the medicine service attending clarifies the intended dose.** This fits if the 1700 mg figure may be a transcription error.\n\nTell me which dose the prescriber wants and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
